	abstract = {The Secure Retrieval-Augmented Generation Framework for Automated Knowledge Access in Enterprise Git Repositories Assistant is a smart system that helps developers explore and make sense of large enterprise codebases using AI. Working with modern software means dealing with massive, complicated codebases spread across multiple repositories. Finding the right piece of code or understanding what it does can feel like searching for a needle in a haystack. This system provides a conversational AI interface that connects with GitHub and uses semantic code indexing to find and explain the exact snippets developers need. Under the hood, it runs on a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture, combining intelligent search with generative AI to deliver accurate answers with real context. The system also includes automated security analysis using AI-enhanced static analysis tools to flag potential vulnerabilities. Built to integrate naturally into existing workflows, whether in browsers or IDEs, this system makes developers more productive by reducing time spent searching through code and accelerating comprehension of complex systems. © 2026 IEEE.},
